3. NOT REDISTRIBUTED — the twelve remaining OOD props
================================================================================

Twelve of the eighteen OOD props are NOT redistributable and are NOT in this
repository, in any form — no meshes, no textures, no cooked packages.

  vehicle.ood.sedan          vehicle.ood.hatchback      vehicle.ood.suv
  vehicle.ood.armoredvan     vehicle.ood.dumptruck      vehicle.ood.roadroller
  walker.pedestrian.soldier  walker.pedestrian.wheelchair
  static.prop.trafficmessageboard   static.prop.trafficarrowboard
  static.prop.europianarrowboardtrailer   static.prop.roadclosedsign

Two distinct reasons:

  (a) Ten are paid marketplace assets whose licences prohibit standalone
      redistribution AND separately prohibit AI use. A seller granting
      redistribution would not cure the AI-use restriction, so no permission
      path was available.

  (b) Two are third-party game IP uploaded to a free model site under a licence
      the uploader had no right to grant. They are not redistributable by
      anyone, including us.

These twelve are specified DIMENSIONALLY instead — the paper's appendix gives
each prop's bounding box and its shift class, and the classifier rule that
assigns a prop to the visual or geometric class is published. See
docs/replacing-props.md. We deliberately do NOT name the marketplace listings:
directing users to purchase assets carrying an AI-use prohibition, for use in an
AI benchmark, would point them into the same restriction that closed that path
for us.

Blueprint IDs for the six vehicles were renamed to the neutral vehicle.ood.*
namespace. That rename removes live third-party trademarks from a safety
benchmark that publishes collision rates, and it decouples the blueprint ID from
the asset's provenance so that a future mesh swap does not rewrite route XMLs.
No trademark claim is made or implied by any identifier in this repository.


